d. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;
e. the right to determine their own decisions;
f. the right to special handling related to victim confidentiality;
g. the right to obtain information;
h. the right to confidentiality of identity;
i. the right to social rehabilitation;
j. the right to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with laws and regulations; andk. the right to spiritual guidance services.

Article 13

Every child has the right to obtain:
a. birth registration;
b. health;
c. education; andd. social welfare.

Article 11

1. To implement Women's Empowerment as referred to in Article 6, the Regional Government shall organize gender mainstreaming including: a establishing the implementation of gender mainstreaming;

b coordinating, facilitating, and mediating gender mainstreaming;

c facilitating institutional strengthening and development of gender mainstreaming mechanisms in government institutions, women's study centers, research and development institutions, non-governmental institutions;

d implementing gender mainstreaming related to the fields of development, education, health, economy, law, Human Rights and politics, environment and socio-culture;

e improving the quality of life of women related to the fields of development, education, health, economy, law, Human Rights and politics, environment and socio-culture;

f integrating efforts to improve the quality of life of women related to the fields of development, education, health, economy, law, Human Rights and politics, environment and socio-culture;

g coordinating the implementation of improving the quality of life of women related to the fields of development, education, health, economy, law, Human Rights and politics, environment and socio-culture;

h organizing the protection of women especially protection for victims of violence, female workers, elderly women, and women with disabilities, in conflict areas and disaster-affected areas;

i facilitating the integration of women's protection especially protection for victims of violence, female workers, elderly women and women with disabilities, in conflict areas and disaster-affected areas;

j coordinating the protection of women especially protection for victims of violence, female workers, elderly women and women with disabilities;

k facilitating the strengthening and development of networks of community institutions or organizations and the business world for the implementation of gender mainstreaming;

l developing a gender-based information system; and m providing and organizing integrated or non-integrated services for women victims of violence, female workers, elderly women, and women with disabilities.

2. Further provisions regarding the forms of women's empowerment and gender mainstreaming mechanisms as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 42

Legal services as referred to in Article 37 letter e are to assist victims in undergoing the judicial process by: a. providing legal consultation that includes information regarding the rights of victims and the judicial process;
b. accompanying victims at the investigation, prosecution, and examination levels in court hearings and assisting victims to fully describe the violence they have experienced; andc. coordinating with fellow law enforcers, volunteer assistants, and social workers so that the judicial process proceeds as it should.

Article 31

Neglect as referred to in Article 27 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to meet the needs of children properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or take care of children as they should, committed by parents, guardians, or other parties responsible for their care;
c. acts of neglecting a person within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or because of an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide life, care, or maintenance to that person; and/ataud. acts that result in economic dependence by restricting and/or prohibiting decent work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

Article 3

This Regional Regulation aims to:
a. guarantee the fulfillment of the rights of women and children;
b. maintain the integrity of the household to realize a harmonious family;
c. prevent violence against women and children;
d. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children; e. provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence;
f. provide protection to reporters and witnesses; and g. empower women victims of violence.

