Article 4

Every Woman has the right: a to life and the right to maintain life and livelihood;

b to form a family and continue offspring through lawful marriage;

c to develop themselves through the fulfillment of their basic needs; d to obtain education and benefit from science and technology, arts and culture, to improve the quality of life and for the welfare of humanity; e to advance themselves in fighting for their rights collectively to build society, nation and state; f to recognition, guarantee, protection and fair legal certainty as well as equal treatment before the law;

g to work and receive fair and proper remuneration and treatment in employment relations;

h to obtain equal opportunities in government; i to freedom of association, assembly and expression of opinion; j to protection of self, family, honor, dignity and property under their control, and the right to a sense of security and protection from threats of fear to do or not do something that is a basic right;

k to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and the right to obtain political asylum from other countries;

l to live prosperously physically and spiritually, to reside and obtain a good and healthy living environment, and the right to obtain health services;

m to social security that enables their full development as dignified human beings;

n to equality of position in law and government;

o to work and a livelihood worthy of humanity; p in the defense of the state;

q to communicate and obtain information to develop their personal and social environment, and the right to seek, obtain, possess, store, process, and convey information using all types of available channels;

r to embrace their respective religions and to worship according to their religion and beliefs; and s to obtain education.

CHAPTER V

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 45

Every woman and child victim of violence shall receive the following rights:
a. the right to complaint handling;
b. the right to have their dignity respected as human beings;
c. the right to receive protection from family, community, regional government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on a protection order from the court;
d. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;
e. the right to determine their own decisions;
f. the right to special handling related to victim confidentiality;
g. the right to obtain information;
h. the right to confidentiality of identity;
i. the right to social rehabilitation;
j. the right to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with laws and regulations; andk. the right to spiritual guidance services.

CHAPTER IV

INTEGRATED SERVICE CENTER

Article 44

1. The implementation of services for women and children victims of violence shall be carried out in an integrated manner by the PPT.
2. The PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) is an integrated part and constitutes one unit with the PPT that provides integrated services for witnesses and/or victims of the crime of trafficking in persons.
3. The implementation of services for women and children victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. providing fast and free services to victims; b. providing protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to health rehabilitation, social rehabilitation, repatriation, social reintegration and legal assistance;
c. cooperating with certain institutions in providing translators and volunteer assistants needed for victims;
d. networking with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of victims and cooperating with witness and victim protection institutions, social shelters or trauma centers owned by the government, community or other institutions for health recovery of victims;
e. providing convenience, comfort and safety for victims;
f. maintaining the confidentiality of victims; andg. providing fulfillment of legal assistance for victims.
4. Further provisions regarding the procedures and mechanisms for implementing the PPT shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

